---
description: Refresh the live design preview after every change
alwaysApply: true
---

Brandon reviews the site from the live preview, not from a description of the change.

The current URL is in the project file `docs/live-previews.md`. After any change he could see — type, layout, sections, flow, motion, navigation, or copy — rebuild that preview from the latest work and confirm the public URL serves the new result before saying the change is done.

Do not leave the preview on an older branch or an older build. If the review site is the hub shell, the preview includes that shell plus every later change. If the URL dies, start a new one and replace the link in `docs/live-previews.md` in the same turn.

Preview deployments of the working branch are authorized. Production release stays separate. If publication fails, report the preview as stale and name the blocker. Do not leave `docs/live-previews.md` pointing at a URL that does not serve the commit under review.
